course: dictionary
lesson: 8389
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. Ruby can be a red jewel, a deep red colour, a girl's name, or a computer language. To find the right meaning, read the words around it. «Ruby stops games an hour before bed now, and the giant pickaxe has gone.» Here Ruby is a person's name, because you cannot stop a jewel from playing games.
explain: Capital letters help too. A name starts with a capital letter, like Ruby. But at the start of a sentence, a capital letter does not always mean a name, so check the rest of the sentence. «Ruby-red» with a dash is a colour, and the dash is a clue that it is describing something.
explain: Always ask: which meaning fits here? Try your meaning in the sentence and see if it still makes sense. If a jewel fits, the sentence should mention a ring, a necklace, or treasure. If it does not, try a different meaning.
fact: A word can have several meanings, so use the context to find the right one.
fact: A ruby is a precious stone with a deep red colour, used in rings and necklaces.
fact: Ruby-red is a deep, rich red colour.
fact: Ruby is a girl's name, and many girls in schools in the UK, Australia and New Zealand are called Ruby.
fact: A ruby wedding anniversary is the 40th one, and rubies are a form of the very hard mineral corundum.
exercise: «Ruby in Perth watched her big brother type his phone code.» What is Ruby here? | A red colour | A computer language | *A girl's name | A precious red stone
exercise: Mum says the ring has a ruby set in gold. What does ruby mean? | A wet bus stop | A girl's name | A programming language | *A precious red stone used in rings and necklaces
exercise: «The sky turned a deep ruby-red at sunset.» What does ruby-red mean? | A precious stone in a ring | The name of a girl | A programming language | *A deep, rich red colour
test: «Ruby's teacher showed the class three questions that settle almost any claim.» Here Ruby is | a stone | *a girl's name | a computer language | a colour
test: Ben's parents are celebrating their 40th wedding anniversary. What is it called? | A pearl wedding anniversary | A silver wedding anniversary | A golden wedding anniversary | *A ruby wedding anniversary
exam: «Ruby is a computer language that programmers use to build apps.» Which meaning of ruby is this? | A deep red colour | A precious stone | *A programming language | A girl's name
